# Dependencies and regenerable output.
node_modules/
coverage/
*.tgz

# Hand-run verification harnesses: c2-c3-verify, runtime-harness*, repo-preflight,
# the schema probes. They drive the built lib/ against a locally installed DSH
# runtime, so they are local development tooling and not part of the published repo.
# Their throwaway workspaces are created with mkdtemp in the system temp dir, so
# nothing from a run ever lands here and no scratch pattern is needed.
.audit/

# Version-compatibility probe trees written by .audit/compat-matrix.ps1: one
# installed harness per supported version, each with its own pnpm store and a copy
# of this tree to type-check and boot against. Rebuilt from scratch on every run,
# and gigabytes large, so nothing in here is worth keeping or committing.
.compat/

# Maintainer notes, kept out of the published tree: RELEASING.md, RELEASING.zh-CN.md,
# REVIEW_AND_SMOKE_TEST.md and PROJECT_NOTEBOOK.md live in here now. README.md and
# INSTALL.md no longer link to them. This path is untracked, which is the only reason
# the rule works at all -- see the note at the bottom. It also means these files exist
# on this machine only: a fresh clone does not get them, and neither does any backup
# of the repository. Their previous copies are still reachable in the pushed history.
/private/

# State this plugin writes into whatever workspace it runs against. This checkout is
# such a workspace, so project_memory_update creates .agent/MEMORY.md right here. It
# is live state that sessions rewrite, not source, so a tracked copy would churn the
# diff on ordinary work. It was briefly tracked; this rule is what keeps it out.
.agent/

# Local noise: debug.log plus any pnpm / npm / vitest failure dump.
*.log
# Only appears if someone turns on tsc incremental builds.
*.tsbuildinfo
.pnpm-store/
pnpm-lock.yaml.bak

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/

# .dsh/ is deliberately not ignored: in a workspace that path holds shared project
# state (dsh-skill-filesystem reads <projectRoot>/.dsh/skills), not local noise.

# A pattern here has no effect on a path that is already in the index. Everything
# listed above is untracked, and that is what makes the rule real. To retire another
# path, run `git rm --cached <path>` first and only then add the pattern -- the
# reverse order produces a rule that looks protective and never fires.

# Not ignored: lib/ is committed on purpose.
# DeepSeek Harness loads a plugin's built entry (`main: ./lib/index.js`) and never
# builds it, so a GitHub-based install only works when the build output is in the
# repository. A linked checkout keeps its own node_modules; `pnpm pack`'s `prepack`
# rebuilds lib/ for registry and tarball installs. Run `pnpm build` before committing
# changes to src/.
